Z||000001||sqoach||07-21-2001||06:15 PM||||I'm not sure the size of that nut. It shouldn't be on there tight enough to need a socket, though. If it is, you might have some problems. Someone asked this question before, but I forgot what size they said. I think maybe it was 24mm? Not sure.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumsig.JPG">          <BR>84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)(take it off my hands for $50)*sale pending*<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)<p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 07-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||07-21-2001||06:23 PM||||use channel lock pliers that nut barely touches the rotor it is just there to hold the bearings on the spindleand the cotter pin keeps the nut from backing out.I suppose you could get a socket or wrench ,but my guess is that you will damage the bearings by over tightning you need to have a feel for this thats why I always use channel lock pliers ||||reg||1
